data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Validated recipe — across@4a41f64d\n\n⚠ Version disagreement: this recipe was validated against `across@4a41f64d`, while the units below are labelled `across@latest`. Both are stated rather than reconciled — a recipe's stamp records what was actually run, and a unit's label records what the corpus holds. Differences inside one major are not always cosmetic: check the recipe's own pins before copying it against these units.\n_human-validated 2026-08-12 by farseen (github: FarseenSh)_\n_source: recipes/across/bridge-deposit.yaml_\n\n**Receipts** — what was actually run, on 2026-08-12, by farseen (github: FarseenSh)\n- checks: attest, test, fork\n- chains exercised: ethereum, base, arbitrum\n- on-chain:\n  - none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.\n- gas: see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition.\n\n# Recipe: across @3 :: bridge-deposit\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-12 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 8 quotes · 9 structural · 7 fork assertions, THE DEPOSIT RUN ON ALL THREE CHAINS. ⚠ The deposit is validated; funds ARRIVING is not — see chains and scope_notes. (This companion printed another recipe's stamp for eleven days while these fields were empty. Session log 2026-08-12; C3 now asserts all four status surfaces.)\n# ⚠ AND V5SpokePoolInterface.sol IS NOT A NEWER DEPOSIT SURFACE. It is fill-side —\n#   executeAcrossV5, V5FillInput, Gateway-executor plumbing. Recorded so nobody later \"corrects\"\n#   this row toward a depositV5 that does not exist. See mistake #6.\n#\n# Sources pinned 2026-08-11 (repo-sourced — SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §6):\n#   across-protocol/contracts @ 4a41f64d676d6d1618b53a0a2d9c72c9c004d599  (pushed 2026-08-10)\nproject_id: \"across\"        # the PUBLISHER name — never carries the major\nversion_major: 3            # ⚠ SEE SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §7. `3` here names the SpokePool interface\n                            #   generation (V3SpokePoolInterface.sol), which is where BOTH entry\n                            #   points live. It is not a semver and not a package major — the\n                            #   contracts publish neither. A third meaning for the axis.\nversion: \"4a41f64d\"         # ⚠ NOT a semver. The pinned commit's short SHA.\ntype: \"bridge-deposit\"\n\n# ⚠ ALL THREE ARE EARNED, AND ALL THREE ARE HALF THE JOURNEY. X6 ran the shipped example's\n# DEPOSIT on each chain — not merely inspected the SpokePool there. But a deposit is not a\n# bridge: the fill is a relayer's action on the DESTINATION chain, settled later through the\n# HubPool, and nothing in this stamp observed one. So `chains` names where the deposit was\n# executed and validated, NOT where funds were seen to arrive. Contrast #11 cctp, which observed BOTH ends — burn receipted on Base Sepolia and mint on\n#      Arbitrum Sepolia. ONE round trip; its second-tier transfer is observed but NOT receipted\n#      (corrected 2026-08-20). See scope_notes and rejected A-REJ2.\nchains: [ethereum, base, arbitrum]\n\n# ── THE DEPLOYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Proxies. ⚠ Each fronts a DIFFERENT implementation, of a different size — see mistake #1's note.#\n# 🔴 F-4 2026-08-15 — NOT READY, AND LEFT THAT WAY. Each chain maps to a bare address, so the\n#   typed table emits a row with no contract name (protocol rule 9): the address is served but\n#   cannot be asked for. permit2 and uniswap-v3 had the identical defect and were fixed by taking\n#   the name Sourcify verifies at each address.\n# ⚠ THAT IS EXACTLY WHAT CANNOT BE DONE HERE. All three addresses ARE verified on Sourcify, and\n#   the verified name is `ERC1967Proxy` on all three (checked 2026-08-15). That is the proxy\n#   wrapper, not the SpokePool behind it. Naming them Ethereum_SpokePool / Base_SpokePool /\n#   Arbitrum_SpokePool would be a real name from a real source attached to the WRONG OBJECT — the\n#   inference already refused once for these same contracts. And recording all three as\n#   `ERC1967Proxy` would be true and useless: three distinct contracts under one name asserts a\n#   sameness that means nothing.\n#   The line stays as it is, with its reason, until a canonical source names the implementation.\ndeployments:\n  ethereum: \"0x5c7BCd6E7De5423a257D81B442095A1a6ced35C5\"\n  base: \"0x09aea4b2242abC8bb4BB78D537A67a245A7bEC64\"\n  arbitrum: \"0xe35e9842fceaCA96570B734083f4a58e8F7C5f2A\"\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"across\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/4a41f64d676d6d1618b53a0a2d9c72c9c004d599/contracts/interfaces/V3SpokePoolInterface.sol\"\n  code: |\n    // ── WorkingExample.sol ──\n    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n    pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\n    interface IERC20 {\n        function approve(address spender, uint256 amount) external returns (bool);\n        function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool);\n    }\n\n    interface IAcrossSpokePool {\n        function deposit(\n            bytes32 depositor,\n            bytes32 recipient,\n            bytes32 inputToken,\n            bytes32 outputToken,\n            uint256 inputAmount,\n            uint256 outputAmount,\n            uint256 destinationChainId,\n            bytes32 exclusiveRelayer,\n            uint32 quoteTimestamp,\n            uint32 fillDeadline,\n            uint32 exclusivityDeadline,\n            bytes calldata message\n        ) external payable;\n\n        function depositQuoteTimeBuffer() external view returns (uint32);\n        function fillDeadlineBuffer() external view returns (uint32);\n    }\n\n    contract AcrossBridgeDeposit {\n        address public immutable spokePool;\n\n        /// The SpokePool address differs per chain and is a proxy, so it is a constructor\n        /// argument rather than a constant.\n        constructor(address spokePool_) {\n            spokePool = spokePool_;\n        }\n\n        /// The bytes32 entry point takes addresses left-padded into 32 bytes.\n        function toBytes32(address a) public pure returns (bytes32) {\n            return bytes32(uint256(uint160(a)));\n        }\n\n        /// Deposit on the SOURCE chain. A relayer fills on the destination; this call does not\n        /// and cannot confirm that happened.\n        ///\n        /// ⚠ `outputAmount` IS THE FEE. inputAmount - outputAmount is what the relayer earns.\n        ///   Pass outputAmount == inputAmount and this succeeds, emits, locks the funds, and is\n        ///   never filled. See common_mistakes #2.\n        function bridge(\n            address inputToken,\n            address outputToken,\n            uint256 inputAmount,\n            uint256 outputAmount,\n            uint256 destinationChainId,\n            address recipient,\n            uint32 fillDeadlineSeconds\n        ) external {\n\n_… recipe truncated for budget — 35644 bytes total, full text at the source path above._\n_Continue it: `web3_fetch` with `cursor: \"recipe:across@4a41f64d::bridge-deposit::body@5968\"` — each call returns the next slice and the next cursor until there is none._\n\n**Citations** (preserved through truncation — degrade bodies, never citations):\n- https://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/4a41f64d676d6d1618b53a0a2d9c72c9c004d599/contracts/interfaces/V3SpokePoolInterface.sol\n- https://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/4a41f64d676d6d1618b53a0a2d9c72c9c004d599/contracts/spoke-pools/SpokePool.sol\n- https://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/4a41f64d676d6d1618b53a0a2d9c72c9c004d599/contracts/interfaces/V5SpokePoolInterface.sol\n- https://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/tree/4a41f64d676d6d1618b53a0a2d9c72c9c004d599\n\n---\n\n### across@latest::SpokePoolFillAdapterTest::testRevertsWhenFillsArePaused\n`across@latest` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0 · as_of 2026-08-11T16:57:28Z\nhttps://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0/test/evm/foundry/local/spokepool/SpokePool_FillAdapter.t.sol#L243-L267\n\n```\nfunction testRevertsWhenFillsArePaused() public\nfunction testRevertsWhenOutputAmountBelowMin() public\n(2 units in this chunk)\n```\n\n### across@latest::SpokePoolFillV5Test::testRevertsWhenOutputAmountBelowMin\n`across@latest` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0 · as_of 2026-08-11T16:57:28Z\nhttps://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0/test/evm/foundry/local/spokepool/SpokePool_FillV5.t.sol#L205-L213\n\n```\nfunction testRevertsWhenOutputAmountBelowMin() public {\n        V5SpokePoolInterface.V5FillInput memory input = _defaultInput();\n```\n\n### across@latest::SpokePoolPeriphery::__contract__~13\n`across@latest` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0 · as_of 2026-08-11T16:57:28Z\nhttps://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0/contracts/periphery/SpokePoolPeriphery.sol#L877-L904\n\n```\n// Sanity check that received amount from swap is enough to submit Across deposit with.\n        if (returnAmount < swapAndDepositData.minExpectedInputTokenAmount) revert MinimumExpectedInputAmount();\n```\n\n### across@latest::SpokePoolPeriphery::permit2\n`across@latest` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0 · as_of 2026-08-11T16:57:28Z\nhttps://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0/contracts/periphery/SpokePoolPeriphery.sol#L154-L189\n\n```\nIPermit2 public immutable permit2;\nSwapProxy public immutable swapProxy;\nmapping(address => uint256) private _permitNonces;\nbytes32 public constant BRIDGE_AND_SWAP_WITNESS_IDENTIFIER = keccak256(\"BridgeAndSwapWitness\");\n+6 more units in this chunk\n```\n\n### across@latest::SpokePoolPeriphery::_paySubmissionFees\n`across@latest` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0 · as_of 2026-08-11T16:57:28Z\nhttps://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0/contracts/periphery/SpokePoolPeriphery.sol#L905-L945\n\n```\nfunction _paySubmissionFees(address feeToken, address recipient, uint256 amount) private\nfunction _isContract(address addr) private view returns (bool)\n(2 units in this chunk)\n```\n\n### across@latest::TronMulticallHandlerTest::__contract__\n`across@latest` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0 · as_of 2026-08-11T16:57:28Z\nhttps://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0/test/evm/foundry/local/TronMulticallHandler.t.sol#L11-L50\n\n```\ncontract TronMulticallHandlerTest is Test {\n    TronMulticallHandler handler;\n```\n\n### across@latest::SpokePoolRelayTest::testCallsMessageHandlerIfRecipientIsContract\n`across@latest` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0 · as_of 2026-08-11T16:57:28Z\nhttps://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0/test/evm/foundry/local/spokepool/SpokePool_Relay.t.sol#L512-L539\n\n```\nfunction testCallsMessageHandlerIfRecipientIsContract() public {\n        MockAcrossMessageHandlerWithEvent messageHandler = new MockAcrossMessageHandlerWithEvent();\n```\n\n### across@latest::SpokePoolFillV5Test::testRevertsWhenSubmitterIsNotExclusiveRelayer\n`across@latest` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0 · as_of 2026-08-11T16:57:28Z\nhttps://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0/test/evm/foundry/local/spokepool/SpokePool_FillV5.t.sol#L265-L296\n\n```\nfunction testRevertsWhenSubmitterIsNotExclusiveRelayer() public\nfunction testFillsWhenExclusivityHasExpiredEvenIfSubmitterNotExclusive() public\nfunction testRevertsWhenFillDeadlinePassed() public\n(3 units in this chunk)\n```\n\n### across@latest::TransferProxy::_transfer\n`across@latest` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0 · as_of 2026-08-11T16:57:28Z\nhttps://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0/contracts/TransferProxy.sol#L67-L87\n\n```\nfunction _transfer(\n        bytes32 inputToken,\n        bytes32 outputToken,\n```\n\n### across@latest::SpokePoolFillAdapterTest::testFillsWhenExclusivityHasExpiredEvenIfSubmitterNotExclusive\n`across@latest` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0 · as_of 2026-08-11T16:57:28Z\nhttps://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/421971bf305a3134ebd20fc24530bb7a5a95ecf0/test/evm/foundry/local/spokepool/SpokePool_FillAdapter.t.sol#L291-L323\n\n```\nfunction testFillsWhenExclusivityHasExpiredEvenIfSubmitterNotExclusive() public\nfunction testRevertsWhenFillDeadlinePassed() public\nfunction testCannotDoubleFill() public\n(3 units in this chunk)\n```"}],"structuredContent":{"intent":"integrate","recipe":{"project_id":"across","version":"4a41f64d","recipe_type":"bridge-deposit","last_validated":"2026-08-12","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","receipts":{"validated_on":"2026-08-12","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","checks":["attest","test","fork"],"chains_exercised":["ethereum","base","arbitrum"],"on_chain":"none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.","gas":"see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition."},"body":"# Recipe: across @3 :: bridge-deposit\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-12 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 8 quotes · 9 structural · 7 fork assertions, THE DEPOSIT RUN ON ALL THREE CHAINS. ⚠ The deposit is validated; funds ARRIVING is not — see chains and scope_notes. (This companion printed another recipe's stamp for eleven days while these fields were empty. Session log 2026-08-12; C3 now asserts all four status surfaces.)\n# ⚠ AND V5SpokePoolInterface.sol IS NOT A NEWER DEPOSIT SURFACE. It is fill-side —\n#   executeAcrossV5, V5FillInput, Gateway-executor plumbing. Recorded so nobody later \"corrects\"\n#   this row toward a depositV5 that does not exist. See mistake #6.\n#\n# Sources pinned 2026-08-11 (repo-sourced — SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §6):\n#   across-protocol/contracts @ 4a41f64d676d6d1618b53a0a2d9c72c9c004d599  (pushed 2026-08-10)\nproject_id: \"across\"        # the PUBLISHER name — never carries the major\nversion_major: 3            # ⚠ SEE SCHEMA-DEPARTURES §7. `3` here names the SpokePool interface\n                            #   generation (V3SpokePoolInterface.sol), which is where BOTH entry\n                            #   points live. It is not a semver and not a package major — the\n                            #   contracts publish neither. A third meaning for the axis.\nversion: \"4a41f64d\"         # ⚠ NOT a semver. The pinned commit's short SHA.\ntype: \"bridge-deposit\"\n\n# ⚠ ALL THREE ARE EARNED, AND ALL THREE ARE HALF THE JOURNEY. X6 ran the shipped example's\n# DEPOSIT on each chain — not merely inspected the SpokePool there. But a deposit is not a\n# bridge: the fill is a relayer's action on the DESTINATION chain, settled later through the\n# HubPool, and nothing in this stamp observed one. So `chains` names where the deposit was\n# executed and validated, NOT where funds were seen to arrive. Contrast #11 cctp, which observed BOTH ends — burn receipted on Base Sepolia and mint on\n#      Arbitrum Sepolia. ONE round trip; its second-tier transfer is observed but NOT receipted\n#      (corrected 2026-08-20). See scope_notes and rejected A-REJ2.\nchains: [ethereum, base, arbitrum]\n\n# ── THE DEPLOYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Proxies. ⚠ Each fronts a DIFFERENT implementation, of a different size — see mistake #1's note.#\n# 🔴 F-4 2026-08-15 — NOT READY, AND LEFT THAT WAY. Each chain maps to a bare address, so the\n#   typed table emits a row with no contract name (protocol rule 9): the address is served but\n#   cannot be asked for. permit2 and uniswap-v3 had the identical defect and were fixed by taking\n#   the name Sourcify verifies at each address.\n# ⚠ THAT IS EXACTLY WHAT CANNOT BE DONE HERE. All three addresses ARE verified on Sourcify, and\n#   the verified name is `ERC1967Proxy` on all three (checked 2026-08-15). That is the proxy\n#   wrapper, not the SpokePool behind it. Naming them Ethereum_SpokePool / Base_SpokePool /\n#   Arbitrum_SpokePool would be a real name from a real source attached to the WRONG OBJECT — the\n#   inference already refused once for these same contracts. And recording all three as\n#   `ERC1967Proxy` would be true and useless: three distinct contracts under one name asserts a\n#   sameness that means nothing.\n#   The line stays as it is, with its reason, until a canonical source names the implementation.\ndeployments:\n  ethereum: \"0x5c7BCd6E7De5423a257D81B442095A1a6ced35C5\"\n  base: \"0x09aea4b2242abC8bb4BB78D537A67a245A7bEC64\"\n  arbitrum: \"0xe35e9842fceaCA96570B734083f4a58e8F7C5f2A\"\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"across\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/across-protocol/contracts/blob/4a41f64d676d6d1618b53a0a2d9c72c9c004d599/contracts/interfaces/V3SpokePoolInterface.sol\"\n  code: |\n    // ── WorkingExample.sol ──\n    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n    pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\n    interface IERC20 {\n        function approve(address spender, uint256 amount) external returns (bool);\n        function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool);\n    }\n\n    interface IAcrossSpokePool {\n        function deposit(\n            bytes32 depositor,\n            bytes32 recipient,\n            bytes32 inputToken,\n            bytes32 outputToken,\n            uint256 inputAmount,\n            uint256 outputAmount,\n            uint256 destinationChainId,\n            bytes32 exclusiveRelayer,\n            uint32 quoteTimestamp,\n            uint32 fillDeadline,\n            uint32 exclusivityDeadline,\n            bytes calldata message\n        ) external payable;\n\n        function depositQuoteTimeBuffer() external view returns (uint32);\n        function fillDeadlineBuffer() external view returns (uint32);\n    }\n\n    contract AcrossBridgeDeposit {\n        address public immutable spokePool;\n\n        /// The SpokePool address differs per chain and is a proxy, so it is a constructor\n        /// argument rather than a constant.\n        constructor(address spokePool_) {\n            spokePool = spokePool_;\n        }\n\n        /// The bytes32 entry point takes addresses left-padded into 32 bytes.\n        function toBytes32(address a) public pure returns (bytes32) {\n            return bytes32(uint256(uint160(a)));\n        }\n\n        /// Deposit on the SOURCE chain. A relayer fills on the destination; this call does not\n        /// and cannot confirm that happened.\n        ///\n        /// ⚠ `outputAmount` IS THE FEE. inputAmount - outputAmount is what the relayer earns.\n        ///   Pass outputAmount == inputAmount and this succeeds, emits, locks the funds, and is\n        ///   never filled. See common_mistakes #2.\n        function bridge(\n            address inputToken,\n            address outputToken,\n            uint256 inputAmount,\n            uint256 outputAmount,\n            uint256 destinationChainId,\n            address recipient,\n            uint32 f